# Lúmina patch for OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl `libpiper/CMakeLists.txt`.
#
# WHY: libpiper builds espeak-ng through `ExternalProject_Add`, and ExternalProject does
# NOT inherit the parent CMake configure. Without forwarding our toolchain, espeak-ng is
# configured for the build host (x86-64) and produces an x86-64 `libespeak-ng.a` that
# cannot link into the aarch64 runtime. This hunk forwards the cross toolchain into the
# espeak-ng sub-build. See CHG-0020 and scripts/5-build_libpiper.sh.
#
# Apply with:  git apply   (or)   patch -p1 -F3 -l
--- a/libpiper/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libpiper/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,5 +41,14 @@ ExternalProject_Add(espeak_ng_external
         -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${ESPEAKNG_INSTALL_DIR}
         -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}
+        # --- Lúmina: forward the cross toolchain into the espeak-ng sub-build ---
+        # ExternalProject does not inherit the parent toolchain file, so without these
+        # espeak-ng is configured for the build host (x86-64). See CHG-0020.
+        -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE}
+        -DCMAKE_SYSROOT=${CMAKE_SYSROOT}
+        -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=${CMAKE_C_COMPILER}
+        -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER}
+        -DCMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH=${CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH}
+        -DCMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PROGRAM=NEVER
         -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS:BOOL=OFF
         -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE:BOOL=ON
         -DUSE_ASYNC:BOOL=OFF
